---
// Why not just prompt an agent, as a three panel strip: you ask, an agent
// replies with paragraphs, decide answers with a value and a probability.
// Each panel shares the strip's four rows, so the faces, titles, what was
// said and the captions line up across. The answer line is the one decide
// printed in the triage-check recording.
import Doodle from './Doodle.astro';
---

<div class="strip">
	<div class="panel">
		<div class="face"><Doodle size={56} face="ask" thinking /><span class="who">You<span>think very hard, then ask</span></span></div>
		<h3>You want a yes or a no.</h3>
		<div class="bubble q">Is this issue ready to work on?</div>
		<p>One question, asked the same way about every issue in the queue.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="panel">
		<div class="face"><Doodle size={56} face="lost" /><span class="who">An agent<span>replies</span></span></div>
		<h3>You get three paragraphs.</h3>
		<div class="bubble fluff">
			That's a great question! Whether an issue is ready to work on really depends on a few things. Generally speaking, a well formed
			issue should include reproduction steps, the expected behaviour, and some sense of scope. Based on what you've shared, there may
			be some ambiguity around the acceptance criteria…
		</div>
		<p>Helpful to read. Impossible to branch on. Now it is writing a parser.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="panel answer">
		<div class="face"><Doodle size={56} face="glad-card" tag="no" tone="flag" /><span class="who">decide<span>answers</span></span></div>
		<h3>You get a value and a number.</h3>
		<div class="screen">
			<div class="bar" aria-hidden="true">task-readiness</div>
			<div class="body">
				<span class="ans"><span class="flag">!</span>ready<span class="flag">no</span><span class="pct">98%</span></span>
				<span class="meter flagm" style="--p: 0.98" role="img" aria-label="98% probability"><i></i></span>
				<span class="exit"><code>--fail-on flagged</code>: exit 2, CI stops.</span>
			</div>
		</div>
		<p>JSON mode gets you the shape. This gets you a number to set a threshold on. The probability is the model's judgment, not proof, and not a confidence it wrote about itself.</p>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.strip {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr);
		margin-top: 56px;
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
		text-align: left;
	}
	.panel {
		display: grid;
		grid-row: span 4;
		grid-template-rows: subgrid;
		row-gap: 18px;
		min-width: 0;
		padding: 28px 26px 30px;
		border-left: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
	}
	.panel:first-child {
		border-left: 0;
	}
	/* decide's panel carries the weight: a faint fill and the biggest type. */
	.panel.answer {
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-7);
	}
	.face {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 14px;
		min-height: 56px;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.who {
		font: 700 13px/1.3 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.who span {
		display: block;
		font-weight: 400;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
	}
	h3 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 20px;
		font-weight: 500;
		line-height: 1.3;
		letter-spacing: -0.015em;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		text-wrap: balance;
	}
	p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 14.5px;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}
	.bubble {
		position: relative;
		align-self: start;
		margin-top: 6px;
		padding: 14px 16px;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-7);
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
	}
	.bubble::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		top: -6px;
		left: 22px;
		width: 10px;
		height: 10px;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-7);
		border-left: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
		transform: rotate(45deg);
	}
	.q {
		font: 400 15px/1.5 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	/* The reply visibly runs on past the box. */
	.fluff {
		max-height: 132px;
		overflow: hidden;
		font-size: 13px;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		-webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 45%, transparent);
		mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 45%, transparent);
	}
	.fluff::before {
		display: none;
	}
	/* A small screen, dark in both themes like every terminal. */
	.screen {
		align-self: start;
		margin-top: 6px;
		overflow: hidden;
		background: var(--term-bg);
		border: 1px solid var(--term-border);
		box-shadow: var(--term-shadow);
		font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
	}
	.bar {
		padding: 8px 14px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--term-line);
		font-size: 11px;
		color: var(--term-muted);
	}
	.body {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 12px;
		padding: 18px 16px 18px;
	}
	.ans {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: baseline;
		gap: 0 0.6em;
		font-size: 24px;
		line-height: 1.2;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--term-fg);
	}
	/* The terminal keeps the dark theme's answer colors in both themes, as the recordings do. */
	.flag,
	.flagm {
		color: #f7666f;
	}
	.pct {
		margin-left: auto;
		font-weight: 400;
		color: #f7666f;
	}
	.flagm {
		--track: #5c6068;
	}
	.exit {
		font-size: 12px;
		color: var(--term-muted);
	}
	.exit code {
		padding: 0;
		background: none;
		font-size: inherit;
		color: var(--term-fg);
	}
	@media (max-width: 860px) {
		.strip {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
		.panel {
			grid-row: auto;
			grid-template-rows: none;
			border-left: 0;
			border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
		}
		.panel:first-child {
			border-top: 0;
		}
	}
	@media (max-width: 480px) {
		.panel {
			padding: 24px 18px 26px;
		}
	}
</style>
